brigade — a shard-aware unit-test runner for Zig
Copyright 2026 The Billy Company

This product includes software developed at The Billy Company
(https://billylives.com/).

No third-party source or data is bundled. `brigade.zig` depends only on the Zig
standard library.

It does deliberately reimplement the per-test semantics of Zig's own default
test runner (`lib/compiler/test_runner.zig`, MIT) — fresh allocator and `Io`
instance per test, leak attribution, `error.SkipZigTest`, error-return traces,
and the "a test that logs .err fails" contract — so that sharding is invisible
to test authors. That parity is the point of the file; the implementation is
our own.
